what is used:
- scripts/run_evals.py: loaded by ../../run.py through importlib (registered in sys.modules as
  `run_evals` so scripts/judge.py's `import run_evals` resolves to the same module). Used:
  load_cases, validate_cases, read_jsonl, completed_keys, _condition_prompt, _parse_response,
  _neutral_cwd, _strip_frontmatter, summarize_scores, WEIGHTS, CONDITIONS. The `run` subcommand's
  loop is NOT used (it derives the prompt from the condition label; see design.md D2).
- scripts/judge.py: invoked as a module (`main([...])`) by `--judge`.
- evals/cases.jsonl, evals/rubric.md: the 14 cases and the rubric, unchanged; the rubric's
  sha256 is recorded with every stamp.
- tests/*.py: run by `--selftest` group `upstream` (unittest, offline).
- .claude-plugin/plugin.json, hooks/, skills/: the plugin `--plugin-dir` loads in the `plugin`
  injection mode; hooks/always-on.mjs reads $CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/.i-have-adhd-always.

reproduce the vendoring:
  git clone https://github.com/ayghri/i-have-adhd && git -C i-have-adhd checkout <commit above>
  (cd i-have-adhd && sha256sum <the files above>)
